 in the United States, Australia, Canada, Europe, and internationally. It offers hardgoods, including skateboards, snowboards, bindings, components, and other equipment. The company operates stores under the names of Zumiez, Blue Tomato, and Fast Times through zumiez.com, zumiez.ca, blue-tomato.com, and fasttimes.com.au e-commerce websites. Zumiez Inc. was incorporated in 1978 and is headquartered in Lynnwood, Washington.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Richard M. Brooks Jr. | CEO & Director | Age 65 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 2K people. Revenue per employee of $387K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $18K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Zumiez Inc. is a micro-cap consumer cyclical business with a $215M market cap on $929M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, with gross margins sitting at 35%.","The business throws off $42M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.00\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 17.8% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 26% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 61% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 25% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Discipline and Rules-Based Execution in ZUMZ Response","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/43/Discipline_and_Rules-Based_Execution_in_ZUMZ_Response_110426125002_1793814602.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793814602.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Zumiez (NASDAQ:ZUMZ) Shares Break Below Fifty Day Moving Average \u2013 Time to Sell?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/zumiez-nasdaqzumz-shares-break-below-fifty-day-moving-average-time-to-sell.html","date":"2026-11-04","timestamp":1793788872.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.84,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Could Zumiez (NASDAQ:ZUMZ) Rebound as Retail Demand Shifts?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/smallcap/could-zumiez-nasdaqzumz-rebound-as-retail-demand-shifts","date":"2026-10-29","timestamp":1793310780.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.331,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Head-To-Head Comparison: Zumiez (NASDAQ:ZUMZ) vs. AutoZone (NYSE:AZO)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/20/head-to-head-comparison-zumiez-nasdaqzumz-vs-autozone-nyseazo.html","date":"2026-10-20","timestamp":1792488535.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Floor And Decor, American Eagle, Zumiez, Arhaus, and Petco shares are soaring, what you need to know","source":"stockstory.org","link":"https://stockstory.org/us/stocks/nyse/fnd/news/why-up-down/floor-and-decor-american-eagle-zumiez-arhaus-and-petco-shares-are-soaring-what-you-need-to-know","date":"2026-11-04","time