d P/FCF 5.1 vs 16.5 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 112% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 19.7% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.8% (vs the 8% bar).","The price implies 29.4% annual cash-flow growth, 41pp less than the model expects."],"prof":["ROIC of 5% falls short of the cost of capital of 10.4%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.29).","It runs a 35% gross margin and converts 5% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 7/9 and cash conversion of 4.00x.","ROE of 4% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.0x equity multiplier).","It spends 0.8% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The company holds more cash than debt.","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.01)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at -1.0% over 3 years, -4.7% over 5 years and 1.1% over 10 years, so the decline is easing.","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded -18.7% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 17%.","Capex runs only 0.5x depreciation (1.2% of sales), so the asset base is being harvested rather than grown.","Its Rule of 40 score is -1, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 25.6%, meaningful skin in the game, and institutions hold 88%.","Insider trading is two-way: 1 purchase and 5 sales over the past year, net $201K sold.","It returns 17.8% a year to shareholders (17.8% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 7.4% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","Short interest is elevated at 15.6% of the float, 4.9 days to cover."],"people":["With about 2,400 employees, each generates about $387K of revenue, in line with the Consumer Cyclical median, and productivity has risen 3.5% a year.","That works out to $18K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.7M (5x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":64,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but it earns less than its cost of capital.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 42, gates 12/26)","Trades 61% below fair value of $36.06","Net debt/EBITDA -4.2x","Piotroski F-score 7/9","EV/EBITDA 8.4x vs sector 11.2x"],"cons":["ROIC 5.5% vs WACC 10.4%","Revenue shrank 4.7%/yr over 5y","12-1 month momentum -35%"],"flags":[],"need":["it earns less than its cost of capital"],"buy_below":30.66,"vc":{"base":36.06,"base_src":"dcf","bear":28.63,"bull":46.88,"alt_median":10.69,"n_alt":2,"gap":3.2789,"dispersion":0.1583,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 328% above the other models' median ($10.69)"]},"med":{"pe":19.2575,"ev_ebitda":11.198,"pfcf":16.4664,"pb":2.375,"roic":0.1281,"gross_margin":0.3475,"fcf_margin":0.0624,"div_yield":0.0228}},"ticker":"ZUMZ","date":"2026-11-06"}